>We were looking for some large SCSI disks and were told about the existance
>of the DEC RH18A disks.  These are supposedly 4.0GB formatted 5-1/4" full
>height drives.  Does anyone have more detailed specs on these and on th RH
>series in general?  What about compatability with OSF/1?

Sounds like a part number we'd stamp on the outside of a box, for which 
you need the magic decoder book to turn that into a part number that
we actually sell...  The description suggests it is:

The DSP5400 as repackaged by some other vendor or something we may
not be selling yet as an RZ disk.  The largest RZ drive I can find
in the OSF/1 SPD and the V1.3 disktab file is the RZ74, which is
3.5 GB.

The DSP series are 5 1/4" or 3 1/2" form factor drives.  The form
factor and size are encoded in the names as:

DSP{3,5}xxx[suffix]

3 = 3 1/2"
5 = 5 1/4"

xxx = Capacity in MB divided by 10.

Suffixes I've seen are:

L = Low profile.
W = Wide SCSI
D = Differential 

I think all the DSP drives will negociate for doing Fast SCSI.

The RZ series are usually DSP drives that we have qualified for use
on our systems.

