Douglas Jones (douglas@dekalb.DC.PeachNet.EDU) wrote:

> Under ULTRIX, the server/port was placed in the utmp/wtmp records
> for LAT logins. Any idea why it isn't under DEC OSF/1.3A? Without
> this being recorded, we cannot do a last and detect where they
> cam from. We can do it for a currently active login via ioctl()
> on the tty. But this doesn't help when going back in time to detect
> where a person logged in from (server/port wise). The internet
> address is recorded.

> Any help would be appreciated,

This was something added to Ultrix in version 4.0, I think.
It turned out to be an extremely useful feature for our 
usage statistics gathering and some system controls for dialup
vs. other lines.  

Prior to this feature being added to Ultrix, we recorded the
lat device by an "lcp -p `tty`" command in a global .cshrc file
that was sourced from the .cshrc file on all user accounts.
(Virtually nobody removes that line from their .cshrc files.)

I am really hoping that DEC will put this back into osf/1 in
an upcoming release.  It is unfortunate that there are areas
where moving from Ultrix to osf/1 seems like a step backwards.
But it is early in the history of DEC osf/1.

mike




