Why do you want to write out the dynamically loaded stuff when you
unexec?  Why not just duplicate what crt0.o does before calling main
(i.e., mmap'ing in the relevant libraries) instead?  Or, better yet,
let the native crt0.o code do its thing normally.  That way, you
benefit from the VM sharing.  OSF/1 / SunOS shared libraries uses
dynamic loading not just to save disk space for the executable images
but also run-time swap space....  If you're doing dld or some other
style of dynamic loading -- for run-time code generation or some other
purpose -- then this comment doesn't apply.

