You just have to edit the setup file for your screen. The file is located
in /usr/lib/X11/xdm and the screen setup filename is usually Xsetup_0.
(The actual name can be found as a resource in xdm-config).

In Xsetup_0 you can put any command to show you a picture on the root 
window. Here is the tail of my Xsetup_0 file, where I use xv as tool for
displaying pictures.

if [ -f /usr/lib/X11/xdm/startrek.gif -a -x /usr/bin/X11/xv ]
then
	/usr/bin/X11/xv -root -quit -viewonly -max /usr/lib/X11/xdm/startrek.gif
fi

