Fred> Do any one of the HX or ZLX graphics boards provide support
Fred> for "Alpha-blending" in hardware? I know that the Kubota
Fred> Denali graphics subsystems provide this feature, but how
Fred> about Digital's graphics boards? I'm interested in AXP OSF/1.

The HX does not have hardware alpha support.

The ZLX boards have hardware support for pixel rendering. However, geometry
that contains alpha color values bypass the built in floating point unit on
the ZLX and instead use the host alpha cpu for performing transforming and
lighting. The interpolation and rendering of alpha pixel values is done on the
on boards rendering chip.

