I was rewriting /usr/sbin/adduser to create a "ypadduser" shell skript and
found two bugs: There are two lines which look like c program comments - but
they are valid shell commands which try to execute files in the root directory:

    if read LSHELL
      then
        /* cin 002 begin */		<--- HERE
        if [ ! -f "${LSHELL}" ]
          then
            LSHELL=`grep "/${LSHELL}$" /etc/shells | tail -1l`
        fi
        if [ ! -n "${LSHELL}" ]
          then
            LSHELL="${DEFSHELL}"
        fi
        /* cin 002 end */		<--- HERE


Anyone who uses the adduser shell scripts should delete this two lines or
change them to comments by adding a "#" at the begin of the line!

	Horst

