You are quite right - one has to can "-DHAVE_SELECT_H" to have compilation
succeed.  The following patch worked for me (don't try using it directly,
all the tabs have been converted) ....

Regards,
Larry Felawka



*** ./src/Makefile.orig	Wed Dec  1 11:11:10 1993
--- ./src/Makefile	Sun Dec  5 07:37:16 1993
***************
*** 122,138 ****
  # directory.
  
  # define your compiler:
! CC		= cc
  
  # define special symbols (system, preprocessor options, etc):
! DEFINES		= -DHAVE_SELECT_H -DHAVE_ULIMIT_H -DHAVE_SETJMP_H \
! 		  -DHAVE_TZFILE_H
  
  # define the optimization level
  OPTIMIZATION	= -g
  
  # define where the preprocessor is:
! CPP		= /lib/cpp
  
  # unproto specific definitions -- use either COMP symbol (second is preferred):
  #SRC		= /tmp/$<
--- 122,139 ----
  # directory.
  
  # define your compiler:
! CC		= cc -std1
  
  # define special symbols (system, preprocessor options, etc):
! DEFINES		= -DHAVE_ULIMIT_H -DHAVE_SETJMP_H \
! 		  -DHAVE_TZFILE_H -Dbsd -DUCB_MAIL=\"/usr/bin/mail\" \
! 		  -DSYSLOG=LOG_MAIL
  
  # define the optimization level
  OPTIMIZATION	= -g
  
  # define where the preprocessor is:
! CPP		= /usr/bin/cpp
  
  # unproto specific definitions -- use either COMP symbol (second is preferred):
  #SRC		= /tmp/$<


