>since
>my documentation doesn't say this should work.  Any good ideas on how to
>fix this thing would be appreciated.  Thankyou.

Sometimes I really hate DEC...  They have left out part of the _XGC
struct from their Xlib.h include file, supposedly to enforce cleaner
programming.  

I made the changes below (see the context diff) by adding some lines
from the MIT X11R5 distribution's Xlib.h, and this seemed to fix the
problem for me. You also need to define XLIB_ILLEGAL_ACCESS to make
this patch visible.  However, since it wasn't in the original include
file, the changes may be somewhat 'dangerous', and I certainly don't
guarantee they will work for you...

-Drew


##############################################################################
#		Andrew Gallatin, System Administrator			     #
#	    Institute of Statistics and Decision Sciences		     #
#	  Box 90251, Duke University, Durham, NC 27708-0251		     #
#		    email:  gallatin@isds.duke.edu			     #
##############################################################################

(note the /renoir/usr/include/X11/Xlib.h is the file that works..)

<2:14pm>kahlo/gallatin:~>diff -c /usr/include/X11/Xlib.h /renoir/usr/include/X11/Xlib.h
*** /usr/include/X11/Xlib.h     Fri Feb  5 09:36:46 1993
--- /renoir/usr/include/X11/Xlib.h      Thu Jan 13 17:38:53 1994
***************
*** 224,229 ****
--- 224,236 ----
      XExtData *ext_data;       /* hook for extension to hang data */
      GContext gid;     /* protocol ID for graphics context */
      /* there is more to this structure, but it is private to Xlib */
+     /* added stuff below this line to get Xgobi to compile        */
+     /* I think DEC is being far to anal... *sigh*             ajg, 1/13/94 */
+     Bool rects;         /* boolean: TRUE if clipmask is list of rectangles */
+     Bool dashes;        /* boolean: TRUE if dash-list is really a list */
+     unsigned long dirty;/* cache dirty bits */
+     XGCValues values;   /* shadow structure of values */
+ 
  }
  #endif
  *GC;


