With the help of dbx, I was able to fix the problems with Crack 4.1f.
If you want to compile and run crack, do the following:

First, make sure you have the following flags while compiling: 

    -DFDES_8BYTE -DLITTLE_ENDIAN -Dalpha


(I know, I know: bytesex shold take care of it, but it doesn't.. )
(The -Dalpha is for the next step)

Next, in ufc-crypt.h, add the following lines (just like Cray):

#ifdef alpha
typedef unsigned long ufc_long
typedef unsigned long long64
#define _UFC_64_
#endif


Finally, in Sources/crack-supp.c, change line 50 to:
    printf("pwc: %-19s ", ctime(&t));


I think these are the only changes I made (but I've been wrong before!)

Ajay

