With the first patch from David J. MacKenzie (djm@Glue.umd.edu) and
more effort in porting, I was able to make XView 3.2 work on
Alpha/OSF/1. 

Where the patch is available...

The patch (diff with XView 3.2 distribution available on x.ftp.org w/o
any patch applied) can be found in
/afs/cs.cmu.edu/user/mjchan/pub/xview3.2-alpha.patch.gz.  on
sunmoon.nectar.cs.cmu.edu.  Use anonymous FTP or AFS (if available at
your site) to get yourself a copy. If there are enough interests, I
can also put there a copy of binaries and prebuilt library (shared
library version). 

About this patch...

This patch brings XView 3.2 to work on DEC Alphas runnning OSF/1.
Apply the patch and use native  C compiler to build. Both shared and
non-shared versions of libxview and libolgx will be built, as well as
XView applications in clients directory.

As I'm only interested in some xview applications (see below), this
patch might not cover all the porting issues. Thus, problems are
expected. If you fix something, please let me know as well.

The XView applications that I have made to work with this port include:

	. olwm, olwmslave, clock , cmdtool 
		They are available in XView clients directory.
	. olvwm 3.3  
	. Ftptool 4.5
	. phonetool
	. contool 3.2 (required root priviledge to install on Alpha)

I've been running most of them (namely clock, olvwm, phonetool,
ftptool and contool) for more than two months now without any
problem. Well, the only thing I need to add in .Xdefaults was to make
scrollbar repeat delay a bit longer:

*Scrollbar.RepeatDelay: 	500

If you make more xview programs work and would like to share, please
let me know too. 

Ming-Jen Chan (mjchan@cs.cmu.edu)


