  >> Does anybody have any sage advice with this - what's the simple thing I'm 
  >> missing?  I mean it can't be that tough?!  Email responses please.

Put the following line in the scripts that are giving you trouble:

  exec >/tmp/`basename $0`.out 2>&1 && set -x

This will direct the stdout/stderr from the script and its children to
the temp file, and turn on verbosity within the script.  You should be
able to figure out what the problem is after examining the result.
