Howdy all,

A while back I asked why I couldn't get logged in to my alpha OSF/1 system
from an NCD X-term.  The Alpha would display the login screen on the X-term,
but attempts to log in made the screen go blank for a moment and then return
to the login prompter.  We were running version 2.1 of the software for the
NCD 16 monochrome terminal.

Among the suggestions were:

 - Check permissions on files such as .xsession;

 - Check 'action when XDM disconnects' and set to Ignore in the NCD's config
   utility;

 - Check the .login, .cshrc, .profile, and .xsession file for errors;

 - Upgrade the NCD software to version 3.

The answer turned out to be the software version.  I eventually was able to
try the login with a color NCD Xterm with up to date software and it works
fine.  Thanks to Peter Derr of Digital Equipment to pointing me in this 
direction.  Others who sent suggestions (much appreciated, BTW) include:

