So, now that I've compiled it, here's the summary:

I did as the README stated.
I took all the defaults *except* those listed below:

..

First time through, eh?  I have some defaults handy for the following systems:
3b1             dnix            isc_3_2_2       sco_2_3_2       sunos_4_0_2
3b2             dynix           isc_3_2_3       sco_2_3_3       svr4
aix_rs          fps             mc6000          sco_2_3_4       ti1500
aix_rt          genix           mips            sco_3           titan
altos486        greenhills      mpc             sgi             ultrix_1
apollo_C6_7     hp9000_300      ncr_tower       solaris_2_0     ultrix_3
apollo_C6_8     hp9000_400      next            solaris_2_1     ultrix_4
aux             hp9000_700      opus            stellar         unisysdynix
cray            hp9000_800      osf1            sunos_3_4       utekv
dec_osf1        hpux            sco_2_3_0       sunos_3_5       uts
dgux            i386            sco_2_3_1       sunos_4_0_1     vax
(You may give one or more space-separated answers, or "none" if appropriate.
If your OS version has no hints, do not give a wrong version--say "none".)
Which of these apply, if any? [osf1] dec_osf1

perl has manual pages available in source form.
If you don't want the manual sources installed, answer 'none'.

Where do the manual pages (source) go (~name ok)? [/usr/man/mann] /usr/local/man/mann
Directory /usr/local/man/mann doesn't exist.  Use that name anyway? [n] y

..

Now you need to generate make dependencies by running "make depend".
You might prefer to run it in background: "make depend > makedepend.out &"
It can take a while, so you might not want to run it right now.

Run make depend now? [n] y

..

Then, the make itself had a problem (warning):
..
`sh  cflags eval.o` eval.c
          CCCMD =  cc -c  -std1 -D_BSD -DLANGUAGE_C  -O2 -Olimit 2900
/usr/lib/cmplrs/cc/cfe: Warning: ./handy.h: 28: Undefined the ANSI standard library defined macro NULL (4.1.2.1(9))
/usr/lib/cmplrs/cc/cfe: Warning: eval.c, line 1674: Incompatible pointer type assignment (3.3.16.1, 3.5.4.1(21))
        value = (double) time(((long*)0 ) );
        -----------------------^

so, I decided to control-c outta this and fix it...(I hate these messages about
incompatible pointer types anyways)


icefog> diff eval.c eval.c.old
1674,1675c1674
<       /* value = (double) time(Null(long*)); */
<       value = (double) time(Null(int *));
---
>       value = (double) time(Null(long*));

(of course this fix should probably have been ifdef'd for osf, but I didn't)

then on with the show...

the rest was ok.
then make test (all was ok).
then su root and make install (all went well).

